content:
PLAN:
Design a dashboard layout with 4 main sections (panels/cards) arranged in a grid. Each panel can represent a key dashboard component (e.g., summary, charts, stats, recent activity). Use a simple responsive CSS grid or flexbox layout for clarity and scalability.

FILES TO CHANGE:
- Public/dashboard.html
- Public/styles.css

FULL FILE CONTENT:
### Public/dashboard.html
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>Dashboard</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css" />
</head>
<body>
  <header class="header">
    <h1>Dashboard</h1>
  </header>
  <main class="dashboard-grid">
    <section class="panel" id="panel-1">
      <h2>Summary</h2>
      <p>Key metrics overview.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="panel" id="panel-2">
      <h2>Charts</h2>
      <p>Visual data representation.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="panel" id="panel-3">
      <h2>Stats</h2>
      <p>Detailed statistics.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="panel" id="panel-4">
      <h2>Recent Activity</h2>
      <p>Latest updates and logs.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
```

### Public/styles.css
```css
body {
  margin: 0;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  background: #f5f7fa;
  color: #333;
}

.header {
  background-color: #2c3e50;
  color: white;
  padding: 1rem 2rem;
  text-align: center;
}

.dashboard-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
  gap: 1rem;
  padding: 1rem 2rem;
}

.panel {
  background: white;
  border-radius: 8px;
  padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
  box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
}

.panel h2 {
  margin-top: 0;
  font-size: 1.25rem;
  border-bottom: 2px solid #3498db;
  padding-bottom: 0.25rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
}
```

RUN COMMANDS:
- Open `Public/dashboard.html` in a browser to verify the layout.

EXPECTED OUTPUT:
A clean dashboard page with a header and four equally spaced panels arranged in a responsive grid, each panel labeled (Summary, Charts, Stats, Recent Activity).

TROUBLESHOOTING:
- If panels do not align properly, check CSS grid support and syntax.
- Ensure `styles.css` is correctly linked and loaded.
- Adjust `minmax` values in grid-template-columns if panels are too narrow or wide on certain screen sizes.

Builder: To add a live clock showing the current time on the dashboard, follow these steps:

PLAN:
- Add a time display element in the header.
- Use JavaScript to update the time every second.

FILES TO CHANGE:
- Public/dashboard.html
- Public/scripts.js (create if not existing)
- Public/dashboard.html (add script reference)

FULL FILE CONTENT:
### Public/dashboard.html
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>Dashboard</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css" />
</head>
<body>
  <header class="header">
    <h1>Dashboard</h1>
    <div id="clock" class="clock"></div>
  </header>
  <main class="dashboard-grid">
    <section class="panel" id="panel-1">
      <h2>Summary</h2>
      <p>Key metrics overview.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="panel" id="panel-2">
      <h2>Charts</h2>
      <p>Visual data representation.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="panel" id="panel-3">
      <h2>Stats</h2>
      <p>Detailed statistics.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="panel" id="panel-4">
      <h2>Recent Activity</h2>
      <p>Latest updates and logs.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <script src="scripts.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

### Public/styles.css
```css
body {
  margin: 0;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  background: #f5f7fa;
  color: #333;
}

.header {
  background-color: #2c3e50;
  color: white;
  padding: 1rem 2rem;
  text-align: center;
  position: relative;
}

.clock {
  position: absolute;
  top: 1rem;
  right: 2rem;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  font-weight: bold;
  font-family: monospace;
}

.dashboard-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
  gap: 1rem;
  padding: 1rem 2rem;
}

.panel {
  background: white;
  border-radius: 8px;
  padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
  box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
}

.panel h2 {
  margin-top: 0;
  font-size: 1.25rem;
  border-bottom: 2px solid #3498db;
  padding-bottom: 0.25rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
}
```

### Public/scripts.js
```js
function updateClock() {
  const clock = document.getElementById('clock');
  if (!clock) return;
  const now = new Date();
  const timeString = now.toLocaleTimeString();
  clock.textContent = timeString;
}

setInterval(updateClock, 1000);
updateClock();
```

RUN COMMANDS:
- Open `Public/dashboard.html` in a browser.
- Confirm the clock appears top-right in the header and updates every second.

EXPECTED OUTPUT:
A live digital clock displayed in the header, showing the current local time, updating every second.

TROUBLESHOOTING:
- If clock does not appear, verify `scripts.js` is loaded and no JS errors in console.
- Confirm the element with id `clock` exists and CSS positions it correctly.
- Check browser console for errors and fix if any.
